      "provenance": "literature_retrieved",
      "rationale": "[Literature audit 2026-11-05 (deliverome-analysis PR 236): site added. The paper (PMID 27622563) was cited by GABRP-internal-27-lit, which filed it under the wrong gene; the audit recovered the real site on GABRA5 at T35|S (numbering: mature subunit numbering (after signal peptide cleavage), between mature residues 4 and 5; construct species: human; paper reports surface: yes, function: not_reported). Paper: \"FLAG (DYKDDDDK) or HA (YPYDVPDYA) epitopes were inserted between amino acids 4 and 5 of the mature GABA A receptor subunit subtypes as needed\". Audit note: Mature 4/5 junction plus UniProt signal peptide (31 aa) = human 35; GABRA4 (SP 35, human 39, already in set) reproduces with the same arithmetic. Tag identity and subunit taken from the Results text superscripts (alpha(4,5,6)^HA with beta2, beta3 and gamma2^FLAG; alpha5^HA with beta3 and gamma(1,3)^HA; Fig 4A alpha5^HA V204I/W280R). Surface = flow cytometry on non-permeabilized HEK293T with anti-tag antibody (Fig 4, S1/S2 Tables). Currents were recorded for the receptor combinations but the paper does not state that the tagged subunit was used in the patch-clamp recordings. The paper does not state that alpha1, beta1, beta2 or beta3 were tagged (alpha1 detected with BD24, beta2/3 with BD17; beta1 reagent unstated), so no rows for those. cDNA GenBank NM_000810.]",
